Report #70: "since quests also scale with the world, i'd like the quest
difficulty to also match your level."

Zone scaling already shows every eligible mob one rank above the viewer
(module-side, PerksUnit), and quest turn-in XP is paid at the viewer's level
(OnPlayerQuestComputeXP, module-side) -- but the quest log still colored every
quest from its authored level. A level 5 quest read gray at 70 while the
wolves beside it showed yellow and the turn-in paid full XP.

The 3.3.5 client colors a quest from the QuestLevel field of
SMSG_QUEST_QUERY_RESPONSE alone (client-side quest cache; WDB, which the
launcher already clears every launch). The module had no way to touch that
packet, so this adds the hook it needs.

Change: PlayerMenu::SendQuestQueryResponse routes the QuestLevel field through
sScriptMgr->OnPlayerBeforeQuestQueryResponse(Player*, Quest const*, int32&
questLevel) before writing it (new PLAYERHOOK_ON_BEFORE_QUEST_QUERY_RESPONSE
PlayerScript hook). The module's PerksPlayer rewrites the field with the same
eligibility and one-rank-above-viewer rule as EffectiveCreatureLevel
(QuestDifficultyLevelFor), including the dungeons-scale-up-only caveat (a
dungeon quest authored at or above the viewer keeps its authored number, same
as the mobs inside), and re-queries every quest in the player's log on
level-up so in-session colors keep up (the client caches quest data for the
whole session, so colors would otherwise freeze at the level each quest was
first queried). Gated by the existing LivingGear.QuestScale.Enable config.
Scaling quests (authored level -1) are left alone -- the client already
colors those from the viewer's level.

Touches: src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/PlayerScript.h (enum +
virtual), src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/PlayerScript.cpp (ScriptMgr
impl), src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.h (declaration),
src/server/game/Entities/Creature/GossipDef.cpp (PlayerMenu::
SendQuestQueryResponse call site).
